  "details": "The avatar ranking system is very good and it helps people hide disruptive or badly performing avatars. However its a shame that everything included on the avatar gets loaded in and counted for the performance rating, as well as affecting the other users performance.\n\nThings like local lights or visual HUD shader overlays or little interactive menus, materials for camera systems, etc. These are things that are included into the performance of an avatar, when they are only used and usually only seen by the user of the avatar.\n\nI suggest adding a check/component to only load in something locally, so it does not affect anyone other than the avatar user, while also not bringing down the avatar performance rating.\n\n(If this is already possible, then I apologize, I attempted to find a way to do this but had to conclude it was not a thing that was implemented yet)",
